                      "title": "Seminar Session: Sabotage During Organisational Change",
                      "startTime": "10:30",
                      "endTime": "11:15",
                      "description": "This session explores why people sometimes resist, undermine or sabotage change within an organisation, even when the change is intended to improve performance, culture or working practices.\n\nThe session will look at the human side of change, including fear, uncertainty, loss of control, poor communication, mistrust and resistance to new ways of working. It will explore how sabotage can appear in both obvious and subtle ways—from negativity and disengagement to withholding information, spreading doubt or deliberately slowing progress.\n\nThe speech will also focus on recognising the warning signs, understanding what sits behind resistant behaviour, and how leaders and employees can respond constructively rather than allowing resistance to derail change.\n\nThe key message is simple: people don’t always resist change itself—they often resist what they believe change will mean for them.",
